  "report": "Updated stage: Three focal accounts directly report Super Saturated (SS) hydration: A04, A08 and A13. These are three credited retailer-review origins supporting independently repeated reported hydration within their respective routines; they do not repeat every specific benefit. A04 describes lightweight, refreshing, fast-drying hydration without a clogged-pore feeling before makeup, but wanted more hydration/repair at night. A08 reports hydration at age 51 alongside tretinoin and other actives. A13 reports retained plumpness/hydration through a 12-hour shift, with oily T-zone, dry sensitive cheeks and mild rosacea, plus less irritation, congestion and perceived oil production. The 12-hour duration and those additional improvements remain single-account reports. No direct negative SS hydration testimony is observable here, but A07’s testimony is unavailable even after retrieval. Formula versions are unknown; the evidence does not establish current-formula performance or causation.\n\nA09 separately reports Avant Guard mask plus SS moisture retention. This is one joint-use account, not an independently repeated or separably allocated SS hydration result. The Small Head mask fit poorly on a very small head, especially around the nose, costing one review star despite the positive retention report.\n\nTexture is mixed: A04’s lightweight, fast-drying pre-makeup experience contrasts with A13’s sticky, shiny, slick experience. A13 describes amount and daytime tolerance as relevant, sometimes going out wearing a pump despite shine; advice that most people should reserve it for night is that reviewer’s generalization. A03 independently supplies a first-hand comparison—Wave is less sticky than SS—but its independence posture is unavailable, so it adds cross-venue descriptive consistency with A13 without secure cross-venue independent corroboration. A03 continues using SS despite stickiness, citing a tentative belief about higher glycerin. A17 has never tried Experiment because it does not ship there; its predicted SS thickness relative to Wave is speculation, not another texture experience. Different amounts, routines and unknown versions could matter, but none demonstrably resolves the texture split.\n\nOther-product evidence must remain separate. A10 reports Buffer Jelly retaining unspecified hydrating products overnight; A14 describes gifted Buffer Jelly’s silky jelly-to-oil texture and two uses mixed into moisturizer, with softer, calmer skin. Neither corroborates SS texture or standalone hydration. A04’s favorable cleanser experience contrasts with A15’s Plasma Wash report of inadequate cleansing, dryness and severe eye burning despite multiple application methods. That is a cleanser conflict, not negative SS evidence. A18’s strong Wave hydration praise and C.R.E.A.M moisture-retention/pilling complaints concern those products. A17’s other moisturizer and active-product experiences likewise do not establish SS performance.\n\nExplicit consequences: A04 narrates ordering SS after introduction through a sister, buying Buffer Jelly for greater nighttime hydration/repair, then buying face wash and the mesh moisturizer. The SS Refill metadata does not establish another narrated repurchase. A03 reports continued use despite a texture disadvantage, not repurchase. A09 deducts a star for mask fit. A13 accommodates shine and advises sticky-averse readers against buying, but narrates no abandonment or repurchase. A14 reports free receipt and becoming an Experiment convert; this is neither a paid purchase nor completed future use after dermaplaning. A15 considered returning Plasma Wash but does not report an actual return; it retains loyalty to an unnamed comparator cleanser. No repeated hydration-driven repurchase reason is established.\n\nEngagement: all eight focal Junip reviews have 0 up-votes and 0 down-votes, with observation times unavailable. Reddit native scores are A03: 6, A17: 7 and A18: 10; each is supplied as material_positive=false and not_interpreted, with engagement observation time unavailable. These values receive no material-resonance upgrade and are not verified experiences, independent people, prevalence or buying effects. Distinct Reddit handles share one Regimen Lab thread; their independence postures are unavailable. Detailed experience and non-user speculation are distinguished; there is no additional bare SS agreement to count.\n\nMaterial context, outside focal counts: hillary_____k’s parent comment (2025-01-16, score 24) reports buying Regimen Lab Level Serum during Black Friday, brighter/even skin and emphatic future repurchase intent—not completed repurchase or SS evidence. Skin_Fanatic’s parent question (2025-01-17, score 2) considers C.R.E.A.M without having tried it. The thread starter asks about advertised Regimen Lab products; actor, date and engagement are unavailable in that context. context_f05862db0ee1dcb8c8c6 repeats A18 exactly and adds no origin or observation. Product-page and native metadata resolve product/variant references but cannot supply missing testimony. A14’s explicit free-product disclosure remains material despite metadata saying rewarded=false.\n\nInitial stage: its membership and separate source boundary were not supplied, so an initial-stage diagnosis, counts or change from baseline cannot be reconstructed reliably. The following counts describe the observable updated-stage focal set only. A07 remains missing evidence, not evidence of no effect; source-account counts are neither origin counts nor event counts.",
  "source_index": [
    {
      "key": "A03",
      "findings": "Reddit Iusedtobealawyer, 2025-01-17, score 6; independence unavailable. First-hand Wave-versus-SS comparison: Wave is less sticky, but SS use continues because of tentatively believed higher glycerin. Direct SS texture, no explicit SS hydration or repurchase. SKU/formula unknown. Shares the Regimen Lab thread with A17/A18; its Level Serum parent testimony belongs to another actor and product."
    },
    {
      "key": "A04",
      "findings": "Junip customer 202931541, 2025-03-22, updated 2025-03-23; votes 0 up/0 down. SS is lightweight, refreshing, fast-drying and hydrating without a clogged-pore feeling, suitable before makeup; more nighttime hydration/repair desired. Explicitly ordered SS, bought Buffer Jelly, face wash and mesh moisturizer. Buffer Jelly brought glowy/clean-looking skin; wash reportedly removed makeup, hydrated and ended breakouts. Combo/sensitive metadata; SS Refill target does not independently establish another purchase or formula version."
    },
    {
      "key": "A07",
      "findings": "Junip customer 122992865, 2025-01-17; votes 0 up/0 down. Original and retrieved body both remain 'undefined...'. Context identifies SS First Time, combo skin and verified-buyer metadata, but supplies no hydration, texture or narrated acquisition testimony. Excluded from substantive counts because evidence is unavailable, not because absence of benefit was observed."
    },
    {
      "key": "A08",
      "findings": "Junip customer 152576810, 2024-02-02; votes 0 up/0 down. SS hydration reported at age 51 with challenging skin while paired with tretinoin and other actives; no texture or buying consequence narrated. Context identifies SS First Time and combo/acne-prone skin. Formula unknown; does not isolate SS causally from the routine."
    },
    {
      "key": "A09",
      "findings": "Junip customer 55537943, 2022-12-09; votes 0 up/0 down. Avant Guard Small Head mask reportedly locks in SS serum hydration: joint mask-serum retention, without separable allocation. Very small head/nose fit complaint costs one star alongside praise. Dry/acne-prone metadata. No explicit purchase, repurchase or remedy action; SS formula unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "A10",
      "findings": "Junip customer 97396127, 2023-07-21; votes 0 up/0 down. Context resolves 'it' to Buffer Jelly: a little as the final nighttime step retains unspecified hydrating products and yields glowing skin by morning. Combo-skin metadata. No named SS co-use, SS hydration/texture testimony or explicit purchase consequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "A13",
      "findings": "Junip customer 231128721, 2024-12-06; votes 0 up/0 down. SS reportedly sustains plump hydration through a 12-hour shift, reduces irritation/sensitivity and perceived oil production, and balances oily T-zone with dry sensitive mildly rosaceous cheeks without forehead congestion. Sticky, shiny, slick texture is accepted; amount and willingness to go out shiny matter. Night-only advice for most people and stickiness-benefit explanations are reviewer generalizations, not demonstrated population effects. No explicit repurchase; formula unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "A14",
      "findings": "Junip customer 344086099, 2025-08-05, updated 2025-08-20; votes 0 up/0 down. Explicitly gifted Buffer Jelly, reviewed after two uses despite rewarded=false metadata. Describes jelly becoming fluid oil with silky slip; a drop mixed into nighttime moisturizer reportedly leaves rosaceous skin soft without redness, irritation or clogged pores. Post-dermaplaning suitability and long bottle life are expectations. Notes unexpectedly small-looking 1oz packaging and declares brand conversion, not paid buying. No SS evidence."
    },
    {
      "key": "A15",
      "findings": "Junip customer 210150638, 2024-11-04; votes 0 up/0 down. Plasma Wash has beautiful silky texture but inadequate cleansing/no foam across wet/dry skin, varied amounts and lathering methods; severe eye burning prompted considering a return, not a completed return. Less moisturized than an unnamed favored glycerin cleanser after one wash and drier after two; unsuitable for this actor’s double cleanse. Defect or misuse remains the reviewer’s uncertainty. Opposes A04’s cleanser praise, not SS hydration."
    },
    {
      "key": "A17",
      "findings": "Reddit Live_Rhubarb_7560, 2025-01-17, score 7; independence unavailable. Never tried Experiment because shipping is unavailable locally. Predicts Wave is thinner than SS from stated glycerin percentages; speculative SS texture only. Actual Wave use includes liking hydrating serums and wanting larger bottles. Zerafite/C.R.E.A.M comparisons, mixing Wave into C.R.E.A.M, extra-layer agreement and reports on other actives/cleanser concern other products. A18 reappears as linked parent context, not new corroboration."
    },
    {
      "key": "A18",
      "findings": "Reddit orchidmommy, 2025-01-16, score 10; independence unavailable. Calls Wave the most hydrating product personally used. C.R.E.A.M reportedly retains moisture poorly overnight relative to another moisturizer and pills under daytime sunscreen; judged unsuitable, without an explicit return or switching transaction. No SS experience. context_f05862db0ee1dcb8c8c6 is this same account and statement."
    }
  ],
